          "EEO / REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS / HARASSMENT / SEXUAL HARASSMENT / COMPLAINT PROCEDURE",
          "EEO",
          "The Company is dedicated to the principles of equal employment opportunity. We prohibit unlawful discrimination against applicants, employees, or other persons on the basis of age 40 and over, race (including traits historically associated with race, such as hair texture and length, protective hairstyles), sex, pregnancy, childbirth and related conditions, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, color, creed, religion, marital status, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, citizenship, disability, military status, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. The Company commits to follow, and provides notice to each of its employees of, the Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies, Colorado Civil Rights Division Anti-Discrimination Laws Notice and EEOC posters, which are posted in general bulletin area at the Company’s offices.",
          "This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including, but not limited to, hiring, training, promotion, discipline, compensation, benefits, and termination of employment. This policy also applies to conduct both on and off DTEC property or work sites.",
          "All Company employees, other workers, and representatives are prohibited from engaging in unlawful discrimination. Any employee, regardless of position or title, who subjects an individual to discrimination or retaliation in violation of this policy will be subject to discipline, up to and including termination.",
          "Reasonable Accommodations",
          "The Company complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws regarding reasonable accommodations, including the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), as amended by the ADA Amendments Act, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act, the Colorado Anti-Discrimination Act, and the federal and Colorado Pregnant Workers Fairness Acts. Consistent with applicable requirements, the Company will make reasonable accommodation for qualified individuals with disabilities, or who need an accommodation related to pregnancy, physical recovery from childbirth, or a related condition, unless doing so would result in an undue hardship to the Company or cause a direct threat to health or safety. The Company will also make reasonable accommodation for an employee’s religious beliefs or practices, unless doing so poses undue hardship on the Company.",
          "Individuals who believe they need an accommodation should submit a request for reasonable accommodation to the Company in writing describing the accommodation requested, the reasons the accommodation is needed, and how the accommodation will help the individual perform the essential functions of the position. After receiving a request for accommodation, the Company will engage in a timely, good-faith, and interactive process with the individual to determine whether there is an effective, reasonable accommodation that will enable the employee to perform the essential functions of the position. Individuals are encouraged to suggest specific reasonable accommodations that would allow them to perform the position; however, the Company is not required to make the specific accommodation requested and may provide any alternative, effective accommodation to the extent that any reasonable accommodation can be made without imposing an undue hardship on the Company.",
