          "Some benefits may be continued at the employee's expense if the employee so chooses. The employee will be notified in writing of the benefits that may be continued and of the terms, conditions, and limitations of such continuance. This typically refers to COBRA insurance. COBRA allows the employee to continue health benefits for up to 18 months after an employee has left DTEC. The terminated employee will be responsible for all premiums related to COBRA.",
