          "The law requires that DTEC make certain deductions from every employee's compensation. Among these are applicable federal, state, and local income taxes. DTEC also must deduct Social Security taxes on each employee's earnings up to a specified limit that is called the Social Security \"wage base.\" DTEC matches the amount of Social Security taxes paid by each employee.",
          "Garnishments- DTEC is required by law to honor any garnishment, assignment, support order or levy properly served on the Company for an active employee. The Company does not have the ability to modify, rescind, or otherwise alter any such requirement to deduct from an employee’s paycheck.",
