          "I have read and understand the above statements.",
          "EMPLOYEE’S NAME (printed):  ______________________________",
          "EMPLOYEE SIGNATURE: DATE:",
          "ATTENDANCE POLICY",
          "Attendance, including coming to work on time, is an essential function of every DTEC position. Employees are expected to come to work as scheduled, on time and prepared to start working. Late arrival, early departure or other absences from scheduled hours are disruptive and must be avoided.",
          "Poor attendance and excessive tardiness may lead to discipline, up to and including termination. Absences or periods of leave taken pursuant to federal or state laws will not be penalized under this policy.",
          "Employees who are going to be absent for a full or partial work day or late for work must notify their manager as far in advance as possible. Employees who must miss work because of emergencies or other unexpected circumstances must notify their manager as soon as possible.",
          "Call in policy: Employees who are going to be absent for a full or partial work day or late for work must notify their supervisor or manager at least one half hour before they are scheduled to begin or report back to work. Employees who must miss work because of emergencies or other unexpected circumstances must notify their manager as soon as possible.",
          "Tardiness: An employee is considered tardy when they are not present at the work site when scheduled to begin or continue their shift. The work site, for purposes of this policy, is the physical place where they were asked by their manager to report for work during their shift. This could be the DTEC equipment storage yard, office, warehouse, or a client’s work site.",
